# Fog settings

option.borderFog=Border Fog
option.borderFog.comment=Thick fog that extends to the edges of the render distance. Helps hide chunk borders and creates a more seamless transition to the void.
option.caveFog=Cave Fog
option.caveFog.comment=Faint glowing fog underground. Lifts cave interiors with minimal cost.
option.bloomyFog=Bloomy Fog
option.bloomyFog.comment=Strong bloom inside fog volumes, simulating scattered light from bright objects, including behind them. Cheap.
option.bloomyFogIntensity=Bloomy Fog Intensity
option.bloomyFogIntensity.comment=How much the fog scatters light around bright areas, giving it a soft bloomy glow. Higher values add more haze around highlights.
option.overworldFogIntensity=Overworld Fog Intensity
option.overworldFogIntensity.comment=Overall strength of the overworld air fog. Higher values thicken the haze and reduce how far you can see.

value.mistMode.mistModeOff=Off
value.mistMode.mistModeBasic=Basic
value.mistMode.mistModeAdvanced=Advanced
option.mistMode=Ground Mist
option.mistMode.comment=Ground-hugging haze. Basic is cheap noise mist; Advanced adds sun self-shadowing with cloud occlusion at higher cost.
option.mistModeOff=Off
option.mistModeBasic=Basic
option.mistModeAdvanced=Advanced
option.mistDensity=Mist Density
option.mistDensity.comment=Overall thickness of the mist layer. Higher values produce denser, more opaque ground fog.
option.mistColorR=§c▍ §fRed — Mist
option.mistColorR.comment=Red tint of ground mist over its time-of-day hue. 1.00 is neutral; lower cools, higher warms.
option.mistColorG=§a▍ §fGreen — Mist
option.mistColorG.comment=Green tint of ground mist. Multiplies the mist's time-of-day hue; 1.00 leaves it unchanged.
option.mistColorB=§9▍ §fBlue — Mist
option.mistColorB.comment=Blue tint of ground mist. Multiplies the mist's time-of-day hue; 1.00 leaves it unchanged, higher values push it cooler.
option.mistAltitude=Mist Ceiling
option.mistAltitude.comment=Maximum altitude (blocks) above which mist cannot exist. Lower values keep mist close to the ground.
option.mistFalloffRate=Mist Falloff Rate
option.mistFalloffRate.comment=How quickly mist thins with altitude above sea level. Higher = thinner layer, lower = mist reaches higher.
option.mistSeaLevelBias=Mist Sea Level Bias
option.mistSeaLevelBias.comment=Shifts the mist base up or down relative to the configured sea level. Positive = mist starts higher, negative = mist starts lower.
option.mistShadowSteps=Mist Shadow Steps
option.mistShadowSteps.comment=Number of ray-march steps toward the sun for mist self-shadowing (Advanced mode only). Higher = more accurate self-shadowing at higher GPU cost.
option.mistShadowStepLength=Mist Shadow Step Length
option.mistShadowStepLength.comment=Distance in blocks between mist self-shadow samples (Advanced mode only). Smaller steps are more accurate but cover a shorter range (range = steps x length); larger steps reach further but can look coarse.
option.ozoneLayer=Ozone Absorption Layer
option.ozoneLayer.comment=Adjustable stratospheric ozone layer. Tints sunlight, sky, fog and bounce, most visibly at dawn and dusk.
option.ozoneAmount=Ozone Amount
option.ozoneAmount.comment=Strength of the ozone layer. 1.00 is a natural column; higher values deepen the twilight blue zenith and redden horizon light; 0 disables the absorption.
option.ozoneColorR=§c▍ §fRed — Ozone
option.ozoneColorR.comment=Ozone absorption of red light. 1.00 is natural; higher removes more red from twilight, lower lets more through.
option.ozoneColorG=§a▍ §fGreen — Ozone
option.ozoneColorG.comment=How strongly the ozone layer absorbs green light. Green is the strongest absorption band, so this has the biggest effect on the twilight hue.
option.ozoneColorB=§9▍ §fBlue — Ozone
option.ozoneColorB.comment=How strongly the ozone layer absorbs blue light. 1.00 is the natural spectrum; raising it dulls the twilight blue.
option.ozoneAltitude=Ozone Layer Altitude
option.ozoneAltitude.comment=Peak altitude of the ozone layer in kilometres. The real layer peaks around 20-30km; higher layers saturate less at the horizon.
option.ozoneThickness=Ozone Layer Thickness
option.ozoneThickness.comment=Thickness of the layer in kilometres. Thin layers concentrate absorption and amplify horizon-grazing paths; thick layers spread it out.
option.ozoneSky=Ozone Sky Absorption
option.ozoneSky.comment=Applies the ozone layer to the sky: view- and light-path absorption on the atmosphere, deepening the twilight blue zenith and warming horizon light.
option.ozoneFog=Ozone Fog Scattering
option.ozoneFog.comment=Applies the ozone layer to air fog: an ozone-aware multiple scattering approximation where higher scatter orders lose more green/red to the ozone bands.
option.ozoneMist=Ozone Mist Tint
option.ozoneMist.comment=Applies the ozone layer to ground mist: near dawn and dusk the mist tint picks up the ozone-filtered twilight spectrum.
option.ozonePlanetBounce=Ozone Planet Bounce
option.ozonePlanetBounce.comment=Applies the ozone layer to planet bounce light: ground-bounced light is filtered through the ozone layer again on its way back up into the sky.
option.sandstormLayer=Sandstorm Sky Layer
option.sandstormLayer.comment=Dust-dimmed direct sun and moonlight during desert storms. Follows the live storm amount.
option.sandstormSky=Sandstorm Sky Scattering
option.sandstormSky.comment=Dusty sky during desert storms. Hazes the horizon and dims the sun disk to match the fog.
option.sandstormMist=Sandstorm Mist Tint
option.sandstormMist.comment=Applies the desert sandstorm to ground mist: while a storm is active the mist tint blends toward the warm dust spectrum.
option.sandstormBounce=Sandstorm Planet Bounce
option.sandstormBounce.comment=Applies the desert sandstorm to planet bounce light: ground-bounced light is re-filtered through the dust layer on its way back up into the sky.
option.vl=Volumetric Fog
option.vl.comment=Adds volumetric fog with light shafts and variable density. Creates atmosphere and sun rays streaming through the fog. Requires significant GPU resources.
option.airFogCloudyNoise=Cloudy Fog
option.airFogCloudyNoise.comment=Subtle cloud-like shapes within the fog, best visible in morning light. Requires volumetric fog to be enabled for the effect to appear.
option.airFogColoredLightShafts=Colored Light Shafts
option.airFogColoredLightShafts.comment=Sun shafts tinted by the glass or leaves they pass through. Produces colored god rays.
option.airFogColoredLightShaftsIntensity=Colored Light Shafts Intensity
option.airFogColoredLightShaftsIntensity.comment=Controls the strength of the color tinting applied to light shafts


