# Mie Fog
option.airFogMieDensityMorning=Morning Density
option.airFogMieDensityMorning.comment=Strength of the Mie (grey, forward scattering) haze around sunrise. Higher values add more haze and make the low sun glow more.
option.airFogMieDensityNoon=Noon Density
option.airFogMieDensityNoon.comment=Strength of the Mie haze around midday. Higher values add more haze to the clear midday sky.
option.airFogMieDensityEvening=Evening Density
option.airFogMieDensityEvening.comment=Strength of the Mie haze around sunset. Higher values add more haze and make the setting sun glow more.
option.airFogMieDensityMidnight=Midnight Density
option.airFogMieDensityMidnight.comment=Strength of the Mie haze at night. Higher values make the night sky hazier and the moon glow more.
option.airFogMieDensityRain=Rain Density
option.airFogMieDensityRain.comment=Strength of the Mie haze while it rains. Higher values make rainy weather mistier and greyer.
option.airFogMieDensitySnow=Snow Density
option.airFogMieDensitySnow.comment=Strength of the Mie haze while it snows. Higher values make snowy weather mistier and whiter.
option.airFogMieDensityBlueHour=Dawn/Dusk Density
option.airFogMieDensityBlueHour.comment=Strength of the Mie haze during the blue hour around dawn and dusk. Higher values make twilight hazier and softer.
option.mieAnisotropy=Sky Mie Anisotropy
option.mieAnisotropy.comment=Mie scattering directionality. Higher concentrates the haze glow around sun and moon; lower spreads it. Default 0.77.
option.fogMieAnisotropy=Fog Mie Anisotropy
option.fogMieAnisotropy.comment=Forward-scattering strength of fog. Higher glows toward sun and moon; 0 scatters evenly. Default 0.50.
option.mieColorR=§c▍ §fRed — Mie
option.mieColorR.comment=Red tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value; lowering it removes red from the haze, raising it warms it.
option.mieColorG=§a▍ §fGreen — Mie
option.mieColorG.comment=Green tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value.
option.mieColorB=§9▍ §fBlue — Mie
option.mieColorB.comment=Blue tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value; raising it cools the haze.
option.airFogMieFalloffStart=Altitude Fade Start
option.airFogMieFalloffStart.comment=Altitude above sea level at which the mie fog begins to decrease
option.airFogMieFalloffHalfLife=Altitude Fade Half Life
option.airFogMieFalloffHalfLife.comment=Altitude above the Mie Falloff Start where the mie fog density is halved


# Materials settings

option.normalMapping=Normal Mapping
option.normalMapping.comment=Whether to use normal maps from the resource pack. Enable for PBR packs to see proper surface detail. Disable for compatibility or performance.
option.specularMapping=Specular Mapping
option.specularMapping.comment=Whether to use specular maps from the resource pack. Enable for PBR packs to see proper metallic/specular highlights. Disable for compatibility or performance.
option.pom=Parallax Occlusion Mapping
option.pom.comment=Parallax occlusion mapping: offsets texture coordinates for real surface depth. Heavy on weaker GPUs.
option.pomShadow=POM Self-Shadowing
option.pomSlopeNormals=Slope Normals
option.pomSlopeNormals.comment=Uses the POM height field gradient to add relief-aware surface normals to lighting. Disable to keep the underlying normal map unchanged.
option.pomDepthWrite=Depth Write
option.pomDepthWrite.comment=Writes POM relief into the depth buffer so sunlight, skylight and SSPT respect surface height. Disable for compatibility or speed.
option.pomShadow.comment=Adds self-shadowing inside the POM height field from the main light direction. Higher sample counts improve quality at a performance cost.
option.textureFormat=Texture Format
option.textureFormat.comment=The texture format used by the resource pack. Most modern resource packs use labPBR, while packs that are designed to work with SEUS may use OldPBR.
option.hardcodedSpecular=Hardcoded Specular
option.hardcodedSpecular.comment=Hardcoded specular reflections for metallic blocks. Uses built-in values for metal-like surfaces instead of resource pack specular maps.
option.hardcodedEmission=Hardcoded Emission
option.hardcodedEmission.comment=Hardcoded emission for blocks like torches and glowstone. Provides built-in emissive lighting without requiring resource pack textures.
option.globalEmissionCurve=Emission Curve
option.globalEmissionCurve.comment=Reshapes emission response (1.0 = neutral). Lower lifts dim glow, higher crushes it toward bright cores.
option.globalEmissionIntensity=Emission Intensity
option.globalEmissionIntensity.comment=Overall emissive brightness after the curve is applied.
option.hardcodedSss=Hardcoded SSS
option.hardcodedSss.comment=Hardcoded subsurface scattering for organic blocks like leaves and wax. Uses built-in scattering profiles instead of resource pack maps.
option.rainPuddles=Rain Puddles
option.rainPuddles.comment=Controls rain puddles on the ground. Puddles form on flat surfaces exposed to open sky while it's raining, in biomes wet enough to actually rain.
option.directionalLightmaps=Directional Lightmaps
option.directionalLightmaps.comment=Blocklight and skylight follow surface normals for deeper contact shading. May artifact at sharp lightmap gradients.
option.directionalLightmapsIntensity=Directional Lightmaps Strength
option.directionalLightmapsIntensity.comment=How strongly the lightmap is skewed by the direction the light arrives from. Higher values give surfaces a more directional, less even lighting.
option.pomDepth=Parallax Depth
option.pomDepth.comment=Controls how deeply POM recesses into block geometry. Higher values increase the parallax effect but may reduce performance.
option.pomSamples=Parallax Samples
option.pomShadowSamples=POM Self-Shadow Samples
option.pomShadowSamples.comment=Controls the number of height-field samples used for POM self-shadowing. Higher values improve detail but cost more performance.
option.pomSamples.comment=Adjusts the number of sampling steps for POM. Higher values increase quality and reduce noise but significantly impact performance.
option.pomDistance=POM Distance
option.pomDistance.comment=Distance in blocks that the parallax effect is calculated for. Objects further away use flat textures instead.
option.refraction=Refraction
option.refraction.comment=Selects how the water surface refracts the scene behind it. The different modes trade accuracy for performance.
option.refractionIntensity=Refraction Intensity
option.refractionIntensity.comment=How strongly the water surface bends what is seen through it. Higher values distort the view behind the water more.
option.dispersionIntensity=Dispersion Intensity
option.dispersionIntensity.comment=Adds chromatic dispersion (RGB fringing) to refracted water/glass, like light splitting through a prism

suffix.pomDepth=m
suffix.pomDistance=m


option.environmentReflections=Environment Reflections
option.environmentReflections.comment=Screen-space reflections on water and shiny blocks. Heavy on weaker GPUs.
option.skyReflections=Sky Reflections
option.skyReflections.comment=Makes water and shiny blocks reflect the sky. Enhances the blue sky reflection on water surfaces for a more realistic appearance.
option.ssrRoughnessSupport=Roughness Support
option.ssrRoughnessSupport.comment=Makes reflections on rough surfaces appear properly rough. Without this, rough surfaces appear mirror-like. Significant performance impact.
option.ssrRayCount=Ray Count
option.ssrRayCount.comment=Reflection rays per pixel. More rays mean less noise at higher cost.
option.ssrIntersectionStepsSmooth=Intersection Steps - Smooth
option.ssrIntersectionStepsSmooth.comment=Intersection-test count for smooth reflections. Higher is more accurate but slower.
option.ssrIntersectionStepsRough=Intersection Steps - Rough
option.ssrIntersectionStepsRough.comment=Adjusts the accuracy of rough reflections. Higher values improve quality but reduce performance. Controls intersection tests for non-mirror-like surfaces.
option.ssrRefinementSteps=Refinement Steps
option.ssrRefinementSteps.comment=Adjusts the refinement quality for all reflections. Higher values improve accuracy but increase performance cost. Final polishing step for reflections.
option.ssrRoughnessThresh=Roughness Threshold
option.ssrRoughnessThresh.comment=Adjusts the roughness threshold for reflections. Lower values reflect on rougher surfaces, higher values only reflect on smooth/mirror-like surfaces.

# Water settings

option.waterCaustics=Water Caustics
option.waterCausticsIntensity=Water Caustics Intensity
option.waterCausticsIntensity.comment=Brightness of the light patterns that the caustics cast onto surfaces under water. Higher values make the dancing highlights brighter.
option.rainRipples=Rain Ripples
option.rainRipples.comment=Expanding raindrop ripple rings on still, sky-exposed water. Costs one texture sample per water texel.
option.rainRippleStrength=Rain Ripple Strength
option.rainRippleStrength.comment=Adjusts how strongly rain ripples distort the water surface normal. Higher = more pronounced, choppier ripples.
option.waterCaustics.comment=Animated light patterns cast onto surfaces under water, as if sunlight were refracted through the moving surface.
option.waterEdgeHighlight=Water Edge Highlight
option.waterEdgeHighlight.comment=White highlights at the water surface edge. Makes water boundaries more visible against terrain, especially in shallow water.
option.waterEdgeHighlightIntensity=Water Edge Highlight Intensity
option.waterEdgeHighlightIntensity.comment=Brightness of the thin highlight along the water surface where it meets geometry. Higher values make shorelines and pool rims glow more.
option.snellsWindow=Snell's Window
option.snellsWindow.comment=Total internal reflection underwater. It draws the bright circle of sky that is visible from below the surface.
option.waterTexture=Water Texture
option.waterTexture.comment=Controls water texture rendering mode. Off: no texture. Highlights: adds RTX-style highlights. Vanilla: uses standard Minecraft water texture.
option.biomeWaterColor=Biome-Colored Water
option.biomeWaterColor.comment=Water absorption takes the biome water colour into account


option.waterWaves=Enabled
option.waterWaves.comment=Enables the animated procedural waves on the water surface. Turning this off leaves the water flat and still.
option.waterWaveIterations=Iterations
option.waterWaveIterations.comment=Number of wave octaves that are summed to build the water surface. More octaves give finer, more detailed waves at a higher cost.
option.waterWaveStrength=Intensity
option.waterWaveStrength.comment=How strongly the procedural waves affect the water surface normals. Higher values make the water choppier and the reflections more distorted.
option.waterWaveFrequency=Frequency
option.waterWaveFrequency.comment=How tightly the wave crests are spaced. Higher values give smaller, more frequent ripples.
option.waterWaveSpeedStill=Speed (Still)
option.waterWaveSpeedStill.comment=Speed at which the waves animate in still water. Higher values make the surface move faster.
option.waterWaveSpeedFlowing=Speed (Flowing)
option.waterWaveSpeedFlowing.comment=Speed at which the waves animate in flowing water, where the flow direction is added on top of the wave motion.
option.waterWavePersistence=Persistence
option.waterWavePersistence.comment=How much of each wave octave carries over into the next one. Higher values make the waves rougher and more chaotic, lower values make them smoother.
option.waterWaveLacunarity=Lacunarity
option.waterWaveLacunarity.comment=How much the wave detail grows between octaves. Higher values add progressively finer detail to the surface.
option.waterParallax=Water Parallax
option.waterParallax.comment=Makes water waves appear three-dimensional by offsetting texture coordinates based on view angle. Creates depth effect in water. Performance impact moderate.
option.waterDisplacement=Water Displacement
option.waterDisplacement.comment=Gently waves water geometry for shoreline movement and a less flat surface. Minimal cost.
option.waterWavesHeightVariation=Local Height Variation
option.waterWavesHeightVariation.comment=Controls local height variation of water waves. Makes wave heights vary across the surface for a more natural, organic appearance.

option.waterAbsorptionR=§c▍ §fRed Absorption
option.waterAbsorptionR.comment=Red component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb red light faster, so deep water loses its warmth and turns blue-green.
option.waterAbsorptionG=§a▍ §fGreen Absorption
option.waterAbsorptionG.comment=Green component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb green light faster.
option.waterAbsorptionB=§9▍ §fBlue Absorption
option.waterAbsorptionB.comment=Blue component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb blue light faster.
option.waterScattering=Scattering
option.waterScattering.comment=How much light the water scatters back towards the viewer. Higher values make the water look milkier and hide what lies behind it.

option.waterAbsorptionRUnderwater=§c▍ §fRed Absorption - Underwater
option.waterAbsorptionRUnderwater.comment=Red component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged, so the underwater fog has its own tint.
option.waterAbsorptionGUnderwater=§a▍ §fGreen Absorption - Underwater
option.waterAbsorptionGUnderwater.comment=Green component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged.
option.waterAbsorptionBUnderwater=§9▍ §fBlue Absorption - Underwater
option.waterAbsorptionBUnderwater.comment=Blue component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged.
option.waterScatteringUnderwater=Scattering - Underwater
option.waterScatteringUnderwater.comment=How much light the water scatters back towards the viewer while you are underwater. Higher values make the water look milkier and reduce visibility.

# Post-processing settings

option.bloom=Bloom
option.bloom.comment=Soft glow effect around bright areas and light sources. Simulates camera lens flare and bright light bleeding. Performance impact varies with intensity.
option.bloomIntensity=Bloom Intensity
option.bloomIntensity.comment=Adjusts the bloom intensity. Higher values increase the glow effect and area affected, but may reduce performance.
option.bloomUpsamplingFilter=Bloom Filter
option.bloomUpsamplingFilter.comment=Selects the filter used to upsample the bloom buffers. Bilinear is cheap and soft, bicubic keeps the glow sharper but costs a little more.
value.bloomUpsamplingFilter.texture=Bilinear
value.bloomUpsamplingFilter.bicubicFilter=Bicubic
option.dof=Depth of field
option.dof.comment=Camera depth of field effect. Blurs areas outside the focal distance to simulate camera optics. Controls how much of the scene is in focus.
option.chromaticDispersion=Chromatic Dispersion
option.chromaticDispersion.comment=Radial spectral fringing scaled by defocus, simulating real camera lens dispersion. In-focus regions stay clean; blurred areas fringe with color.
option.chromaticDispersionStrength=Dispersion Strength
option.chromaticDispersionStrength.comment=Adjusts the strength of the chromatic dispersion fringing. Higher values widen the red/blue separation in out-of-focus areas.
option.dofSamples=DoF Samples
option.dofSamples.comment=Number of samples for depth of field calculation. Higher values produce a smoother blur but increase performance cost.
option.dofFocus=DoF Focus
option.dofMaxRadius=DoF Max Radius
option.dofMaxRadius.comment=Caps the circle of confusion as a fraction of screen height. Lower values keep backgrounds sharper and save performance; higher values allow creamier blur.
option.dofFocus.comment=Focal distance for depth of field. Controls the distance from the camera that appears in focus. Objects closer or further than this distance will be blurred.
option.motionBlur=Motion Blur
option.motionBlur.comment=Cinematic motion blur effect. Simulates camera shutter speed. Helpful for smoothing low framerates but can cause motion sickness in some users.
option.motionBlurSamples=Motion Blur Samples
option.motionBlurSamples.comment=Number of samples along the motion trail. Higher values give smoother streaks at higher GPU cost.
option.motionBlurScale=Motion Blur Scale
option.motionBlurScale.comment=Artistic multiplier on the shutter-driven trail length. Shutter speed sets the physical baseline; this scales it.
option.lensFlare=Lens Flare
option.lensFlare.comment=Ghosts, halo and anamorphic streak from bright lights scattering inside the lens. Computed pre-tonemap so flare grades with the scene.
option.lensFlareHalo=Flare Halo
option.lensFlareHalo.comment=Halo ring around the sun on top of the ghost chain.
option.lensFlareIntensity=Flare Intensity
option.lensFlareIntensity.comment=Overall strength of ghosts, halo and streak.
option.lensFlareThresh=Flare Threshold
option.lensFlareThresh.comment=Scene luminance above which highlights seed flare. Lower values let lamps and glints flare; higher isolates the sun.
option.lensFlareGhosts=Ghost Count
option.lensFlareGhosts.comment=Number of ghosts strung along the sun axis. More ghosts cost performance.
option.lensFlareSpacing=Ghost Spacing
option.lensFlareSpacing.comment=Spacing of the ghost chain along the sun-to-center axis.
option.lensFlareHaloRadius=Halo Radius
option.lensFlareHaloRadius.comment=Radius of the halo ring around the sun.
option.lensFlareHaloWidth=Halo Width
option.lensFlareHaloWidth.comment=Width of the soft halo ring drawn around the sun. Higher values make the halo thicker and softer.
option.camSensorWidth=Sensor Width
option.camSensorWidth.comment=Camera sensor width in millimetres. Larger sensors give shallower depth of field at the same aperture.
option.camFstops=Aperture F-Stops
option.camFstops.comment=Lens aperture. Low values (f/0.8) give razor-thin focus; high values (f/16) keep the scene sharp deep into the distance.
option.camShutterSpeed=Shutter Speed
option.camShutterSpeed.comment=Camera shutter speed as 1/N seconds. Slower speeds streak motion blur longer; 1/60 matches the old neutral look.
option.camIso=ISO Sensitivity
option.camIso.comment=Sensor sensitivity. Doubling ISO doubles exposure brightness across manual and auto exposure alike.
option.camExposureCompensation=Exposure Compensation
option.camExposureCompensation.comment=EV compensation dial for the exposure triangle. Brightens or darkens around the aperture/shutter/ISO result, like aperture-priority mode on a real camera.
option.taa=TAA
option.taa.comment=Temporal anti-aliasing over multiple frames. Reduces flicker but can ghost on fast motion. Required for TAAU.
option.fxaa=FXAA Pass
option.fxaa.comment=Fast approximate anti-aliasing. Softens edges and reduces aliasing with minimal performance impact. Works in conjunction with TAA to improve motion clarity.
option.taau=TAA Upscaling
option.taau.comment=Renders below native resolution and upscales with TAA. Much faster, with some loss of sharpness and stability.
option.taauRenderScale=TAAU Render Scale
option.taauRenderScale.comment=Internal render resolution for TAA upscaling, as a fraction of screen size. Lower is faster but softer.
option.taaIntensity=TAA Intensity
option.taaIntensity.comment=How much of the previous frame the temporal anti-aliasing keeps. Higher is smoother but ghosts more on fast motion, lower is sharper but flickers more.
option.cas=Image Sharpening
option.cas.comment=Contrast-adaptive sharpening. Sharpens the final image to recover detail lost from anti-aliasing. Adjust intensity to avoid halo artifacts.
option.casIntensity=Sharpening Intensity
option.casIntensity.comment=Strength of the image sharpening. Higher recovers more detail but can show halo artifacts around edges.
option.vignette=Vignette
option.vignette.comment=Darkens the edges of the screen (vignetting effect). Simulates camera lens natural darkening at the corners.
option.vignetteIntensity=Vignette Intensity
option.vignetteIntensity.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the vignette effect. Higher values increase the darkening at screen edges.
option.vignetteStart=Vignette Start
option.vignetteStart.comment=Radial distance from screen center where the vignette falloff begins.
option.vignetteEnd=Vignette End
option.vignetteEnd.comment=Radial distance where the vignette reaches full strength.
option.vignetteExponent=Vignette Rolloff
option.vignetteExponent.comment=Shapes the vignette falloff curve. Higher values concentrate darkening toward the corners.

value.dofFocus.-1.0=Automatic

option.tonemap=Tonemap Operator
option.tonemap.comment=Selects the tonemapping operator. Tonemapping compresses the very bright values of the scene into the range a display can show, and every operator has its own highlight roll-off and colour response.

value.tonemap.tonemapAcesFit=ACES Fit
