# Distance View

option.distanceView=Enabled
option.distanceView.comment=Renders the scene from a far distance so you can spot landmarks that are too far away to reach. It is meant for scouting, not for playing.
option.distanceViewMethod=Method
option.distanceViewMethod.comment=Selects what the distance view uses to place the far away scene. Distance places it by its real distance, Depth uses the depth buffer instead.
option.distanceViewMaxDistance=Max Distance
option.distanceViewMaxDistance.comment=Furthest distance the distance view shows. Objects beyond it are not drawn at all.
suffix.distanceViewMaxDistance=m


# Box

option.boxMode=Mode
option.boxMode.comment=Controls the selection box mode. Default: standard colored box. Custom Color: use a custom RGB color. Rainbow: cycling color effect.
option.boxColorR=§c▍ §fRed
option.boxColorR.comment=Red component of the selection box outline colour.
option.boxColorG=§a▍ §fGreen
option.boxColorG.comment=Green component of the selection box outline colour.
option.boxColorB=§9▍ §fBlue
option.boxColorB.comment=Blue component of the selection box outline colour.
option.boxEmission=Emission
option.boxEmission.comment=Scales emission color past value 1.0. Requires bloom to be enabled for the effect to be visible.
option.boxLineWidth=Line Width
option.boxLineWidth.comment=Thickness in pixels of the selection box outline. Higher values draw a thicker box.

# Distant Horizons

option.dhOverdrawDistance=Overdraw Distance
option.dhOverdrawDistance.comment=How far beyond the camera Distant Horizons keeps rendering terrain, in blocks. Higher values let distant terrain keep their detail for longer.
option.dhOverdrawFadeLength=Overdraw Fade Length
option.dhOverdrawFadeLength.comment=Distance over which the Distant Horizons overdraw fades out, in blocks. It blends the extra terrain into the normal render distance.
option.noiseOnDhTerrain=Noise on DH Terrain
option.noiseOnDhTerrain.comment=Adds fine noise to Distant Horizons terrain so it does not look unnaturally smooth. It costs a little extra performance.

screen.indirectLight=Indirect Light
screen.aa=Anti-Aliasing
screen.motionBlur=Motion Blur
screen.dof=Depth of field
screen.vignette=Vignette
screen.bloom=Bloom

# ---- Moon Phase Influence ----
option.moonPhaseInfluenceIntensity=Moon Phase Influence Intensity
option.moonPhaseInfluenceIntensity.comment=Adjusts how strongly the current moon phase affects all moon-phased effects below. 0 = no effect, 1 = full effect.
option.moonPhaseNightAtmosphere=Moon-Phased Night Atmosphere
option.moonPhaseNightAtmosphere.comment=When enabled, fog and sky atmosphere at night vary with the lunar cycle.
option.moonPhaseNightAtmosphereIntensity=Night Atmosphere Intensity
option.moonPhaseNightAtmosphereIntensity.comment=Adjusts how strongly the moon phase affects atmospheric fog brightness at night.
option.moonPhaseReflections=Moon-Phased Reflections
option.moonPhaseReflections.comment=When enabled, the brightness and color of reflections vary with the lunar cycle.
option.moonPhaseReflectionsIntensity=Reflections Intensity
option.moonPhaseReflectionsIntensity.comment=Adjusts how strongly the moon phase affects reflection brightness at night.




screen.ssptFilter=SVGF Filter

# ---- SSPT ----
option.ssptEnabled=SSPT
option.ssptEnabled.comment=Screen-space path traced emission and colored lighting. Big performance impact.
option.ssptFullRangeRT=Long Range SSPT
option.ssptFullRangeRT.comment=Traces the whole screen instead of a short range. Needs more samples for similar quality.
option.indirectResReduction=Indirect Lighting Res
option.indirectResReduction.comment=Resolution of the SSPT trace and filter buffers, relative to the screen. Lower = faster but softer indirect light.
value.indirectResReduction.1=100%
value.indirectResReduction.2=50%
value.indirectResReduction.3=33%
value.indirectResReduction.4=25%
option.ssptSPP=Samples per Pixel
option.ssptSPP.comment=Paths traced per pixel per frame. More samples = less noise, more cost.
option.ssptBounces=Bounces
option.ssptBounces.comment=Path bounces per sample. More bounces = more colored light bleed.
option.ssptEmissionDistance=Emission Distance
option.ssptEmissionDistance.comment=How far colored emission carries before fading out (blocks).
option.ssptLightmapBlend=Lightmap Blending
option.ssptLightmapBlend.comment=How strongly the vanilla lightmap blocklight blends into the SSPT accumulation.
option.ssptEmissionMode=Emission Mode
option.ssptEmissionMode.comment=Emission source used by SSPT. Only affects SSPT.
value.ssptEmissionMode.0=Hardcoded
value.ssptEmissionMode.1=Hardcoded + LabPBR
value.ssptEmissionMode.2=LabPBR Only
option.ssptIntensity=Emission Intensity
option.ssptIntensity.comment=Global brightness multiplier for the emission contribution of the indirect lighting pass.
option.indirectLightingIntensity=Indirect Lighting Intensity
option.indirectLightingIntensity.comment=Brightness multiplier for indirect lighting: skylight and the sun/moon bounce. Emission is not affected.
option.framingTool=Framing Tool
option.framingTool.comment=Master toggle for composition guides (rule-of-thirds, aspect box, safe area). For lining up screenshots.
option.framingThirds=Thirds Grid
option.framingThirds.comment=Overlays a rule-of-thirds grid on the screen so you can line up shots against the thirds.
option.framingAspect=Aspect Guides
option.framingAspect.comment=Target aspect-ratio box and safe-area guides. It frames the screen so you can check how the shot will be cropped.
option.framingOpacity=Guide Opacity
option.framingOpacity.comment=Opacity of the framing guides. Higher values make the guides easier to see against the scene.
option.framingLineWidth=Line Width
option.framingLineWidth.comment=Thickness in pixels of the framing guides. Higher values draw thicker lines.
option.framingAspectRatio=Aspect Ratio
option.framingAspectRatio.comment=Target aspect ratio (width over height) for the crop box.
option.framingSafeArea=Safe Area
option.framingSafeArea.comment=Centered safe-area fraction shown inside the aspect box.
option.maxFrames=Max Accumulated Frames
option.maxFrames.comment=Temporal history length. Higher = smoother, but more ghosting.
option.svgfFilter=Filtering
option.svgfFilter.comment=SVGF a-trous filter: removes the remaining SSPT noise edge-aware.
option.svgfRad=Filter Radius
option.svgfRad.comment=Tap radius of each a-trous filter iteration.
option.svgfStrictness=Luminance Strictness
option.svgfStrictness.comment=How aggressively the filter preserves brightness differences.
option.svgfNormalexp=Normal Weight
option.svgfNormalexp.comment=How strongly surface normal differences block filtering across edges.

option.fogSmoothing=Fog Smoothing
option.fogSmoothing.comment=Edge-aware blur on the fog buffer against blocky artifacts. Current-frame only, so no smearing on fast movement. Cheap.
option.fogSmoothingRadius=Fog Blur Radius
option.fogSmoothingRadius.comment=Fog blur radius. Higher is softer at higher cost, while respecting hard density edges.
option.netherSmoke=Nether Smoke
option.netherSmoke.comment=Turbulent Nether smoke replacing the flat fog glow, with ember-bright proximity glow. Falls back to classic fog when off.
option.netherSmokeIntensity=Nether Smoke Intensity
option.netherSmokeIntensity.comment=Brightness multiplier for the Nether Smoke v2 glow/emission. Only has an effect when Nether Smoke is enabled.



option.materialMappingMode=Material Mapping Mode
option.materialMappingMode.comment=PBR source for materials: off, built-in per-block values, specular map only, normal map only, or both (labPBR/OldSchoolPBR).


option.textureAo=Texture AO
option.textureAo.comment=Lightmap occlusion from the pack's normal map. Needs a normal-mapped pack; inert on vanilla. Off by default.

option.porosityMode=Porosity Mode
option.porosityMode.comment=Wetness source: off, built-in per-block porosity, or the pack's specular map with no vanilla fallback.
value.porosityMode.porosityOff=Off
value.porosityMode.porosityHardcoded=Hardcoded
value.porosityMode.porosityMaps=LabPBR
option.porosityStrength=Porosity Strength
option.porosityStrength.comment=How strongly porous blocks darken and absorb light. Higher values deepen the darkening of sponges, moss and similar blocks.
option.sssMode=Subsurface Scattering Mode
option.sssMode.comment=Subsurface scattering source: off, built-in leaf profiles, or the pack's specular map with no vanilla fallback.
value.sssMode.sssOff=Off
value.sssMode.sssHardcoded=Hardcoded
value.sssMode.sssMaps=LabPBR
option.sssSheen=Subsurface Sheen
option.sssSheen.comment=Specular "sheen" effect on plants and leaves, helps tall grass and stuff to blend better with the grass specular.
option.sssSheenIntensity=Subsurface Sheen Intensity
option.sssSheenIntensity.comment=Brightness multiplier for the subsurface sheen effect.


option.fxaaIntensity=FXAA Strength
option.fxaaIntensity.comment=Adjusts the strength of fast approximate anti-aliasing. Higher = smoother edges but softer image.


option.waterWavesNoiseStrength=Water Waves Noise Strength
option.waterWavesNoiseStrength.comment=Strength of the noise that modulates the wave heights. Higher values make the surface motion more irregular and less uniform.
option.rainPuddlesIntensity=Rain Puddles Intensity
option.rainPuddlesIntensity.comment=How strongly rain puddles darken and wet the ground. Higher values make puddles more visible and more reflective.
option.waterTextureIntensity=Water Texture Intensity
option.waterTextureIntensity.comment=Strength of the resource pack's water texture. Higher values make the water texture more visible on the surface.
option.snellsWindowIntensity=Snell's Window Intensity
option.snellsWindowIntensity.comment=Brightness of Snell's window, the bright circle of sky that is visible from underwater when looking up. Higher values make it more pronounced.
option.biomeWaterColorIntensity=Biome Water Color Intensity
option.biomeWaterColorIntensity.comment=How strongly the biome's water colour tints the water surface. Higher values make each biome's water more distinct.
option.borderFogIntensity=Border Fog Intensity
option.borderFogIntensity.comment=How strongly the haze that creeps in from the edge of the render distance grows. Higher values hide the border of the loaded world more.
option.caveFogIntensity=Cave Fog Intensity
option.caveFogIntensity.comment=How dense the fog is inside caves and underground. Higher values hide distant cave geometry in haze.
option.desertSandstormIntensity=Desert Sandstorm Intensity
option.desertSandstormIntensity.comment=How strong the desert sandstorm looks. Higher values hide the sun further and thicken the airborne dust.
option.rainbowsIntensity=Rainbow Visibility
option.rainbowsIntensity.comment=Adjusts the opacity and vividness of rainbows during/after rain. Higher = brighter, more saturated rainbow.
option.planetBounceIntensity=Planet Bounce Intensity
option.renderBelowHorizon=Render Below Horizon
option.renderBelowHorizon.comment=Renders the planet ground disc for below-horizon rays instead of stretching the horizon sky downward.
option.renderBelowHorizonIntensity=Below Horizon Brightness
option.renderBelowHorizonIntensity.comment=Brightness of the planet ground rendered below the horizon.
option.planetBounceIntensity.comment=Adjusts the strength of ground-bounced light re-entering the sky. Higher = brighter, warmer horizon glow; 0 disables the contribution entirely.

